# {{project_name}}

A subscription contract that charges a recurring amount after each interval
elapses, generated by
[soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge) from the
`subscription` template.

## How it works

The contract bills one plan — a token, an amount and an interval — and never
takes custody of subscriber funds:

1. **Approve** — the subscriber calls `approve` on the token, granting this
   contract an allowance covering as many periods as they want to pre-pay.
2. **`subscribe`** — the first period is charged immediately and the next
   charge becomes due one interval later.
3. **`charge(subscriber)`** — the merchant collects a period once it is due;
   the amount moves straight from the subscriber to the merchant via
   `transfer_from`.
4. **`cancel`** — the subscriber deactivates the subscription at any time.
   Revoking the token allowance also stops payments on its own.

Each charge advances the due date by exactly one interval, so a merchant
cannot bill twice for the same period, and a late charge does not silently
skip one — two owed periods are collected with two calls.

## Interface

| function                                       | description                          |
|------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| `initialize(merchant, token, amount, interval)` | configure the plan                   |
| `subscribe(subscriber)`                        | opt in and pay the first period       |
| `charge(subscriber)`                           | collect a period once it is due       |
| `cancel(subscriber)`                           | stop future charges                   |
| `is_due(subscriber)` / `is_active(subscriber)`  | whether a charge would succeed        |
| `subscription(subscriber)`                     | state: `active`, `next_charge`, `charges` |

## Develop

```sh
cargo test                 # run unit tests
stellar contract build     # build the deployable wasm
```

## Deploy to testnet

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

Configure the plan:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <MERCHANT> \
  --network testnet \
  -- initialize \
  --merchant <MERCHANT_ADDRESS> \
  --token <TOKEN_ADDRESS> \
  --amount 100 \
  --interval 2592000
```

The subscriber approves the contract for three periods, then subscribes:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <TOKEN_ADDRESS> \
  --source-account <SUBSCRIBER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- approve \
  --from <SUBSCRIBER_ADDRESS> \
  --spender <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --amount 300 \
  --expiration_ledger <LEDGER>

stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <SUBSCRIBER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- subscribe --subscriber <SUBSCRIBER_ADDRESS>
```

Once an interval has elapsed the merchant collects:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <MERCHANT> \
  --network testnet \
  -- charge --subscriber <SUBSCRIBER_ADDRESS>
```

